;; flint.deps's own workspace, separate from the stdlib's blanket flint/flint
;; (`DECISIONS.md#flint-deps-is-its-own-workspace`).
;;
;; GOVERNS FOUR FILES BY NAMESPACE PREFIX ("flint/deps"), not by directory
;; containment: `flint.deps` itself is `lib/flint/deps.cljc`, a SIBLING of
;; this directory, not a file inside it. Every door that builds a compile
;; spec has to read this one file and apply that prefix itself --
;; `cli/build.rs` + `cli/src/main.rs` (native), `sdks/esm/src/flint.js`
;; (npm/wasm), and `bin/flint` (bb) -- because workspace identity is assigned
;; per source ROOT in two of those and per namespace PREFIX in the other two;
;; see `DECISIONS.md#flint-deps-is-its-own-workspace` for how each applies it
;; and `AGENTS.md` "one fact, four front doors" for why each needed its own
;; patch rather than one shared one.
;;
;; NO GRANT. `flint.deps`/`flint.deps.manifest`/`flint.deps.registry` are pure
;; data manipulation (`clojure.edn`/`clojure.string` over `deps.edn`,
;; `package.json`, `pom.xml`, a registry document) -- no `:host`-guarded
;; builtin, no virtual namespace require. `flint.deps.resolve` requires the
;; virtual `flint.deps.npm`/`-git`/`-mvn`, but reaching a virtual namespace is
;; gated by a RUNTIME `:with` grant the host checks when the port is opened
;; (`doc/api-review.md`'s "Served, not linked" section), not by this
;; compile-time workspace mechanism -- so this workspace needs nothing from
;; `:flint/capabilities-grant` either. Inheriting `flint/flint`'s `[:host]`
;; for free, as these four files did before this file existed, would have
;; been a grant none of them asked for.
{:flint/workspace flint/deps}
